  "markdown_content": "## Program Announcement\\nThe Indian School of Business (ISB) has unveiled the latest batch of healthcare startups selected for its I-HEAL healthcare accelerator program. Now in its third iteration, I-HEAL @ ISB 3.0 welcomes 15 promising startups that are leveraging technology and innovation to address critical challenges in India's healthcare sector.\\n\\n## Focus Areas\\nThese startups span various healthcare domains including:\\n* Telemedicine\\n* Medical devices\\n* Healthcare delivery\\n* Digital health solutions\\n\\nThe selected companies will receive mentorship, networking opportunities, and strategic guidance to scale their solutions.\\n\\n## Program Objectives\\nThe program aims to foster innovation in healthcare while making quality medical care more accessible and affordable across India. Selected startups will work closely with industry experts, healthcare professionals, and business leaders during the acceleration period.",
